#X text 240 83 the object routes incoming messages to the outlets according
to the match list;
#X text 240 123 if no match occurred \, the original message is sent
to the last outlet;
#X text 240 163 if a route starts with '*' \, the output includes the
message selector \, otherwise the selector is removed;
#X text 240 203 the object can be used to dispatch messages by selector
or by the first list element \, for example to route "note" \, "ctlin"
or numeric messages to different destinations;
